The following body is established: the Advisory Committee for the Coordination of Social Security Systems (hereinafter referred to as "Advisory Committee"). This Committee is made up of one government representative, one trade union representative, and one employer organisation representative from each country in the EU.

For each of these groups, one alternate member is also appointed in each country. The members and alternate members of the Committee have the following responsibilities:

- Collect the data needed and perform the calculations required to prepare each country’s annual report on social security claims;  
- Provide the Administrative Commission with regular updates on the implementation of this regulation and the implementing rules, especially regarding financial matters;  
- Supply the Administrative Commission with the data and reports needed to make decisions under Article 72(g);  
- Offer any relevant suggestions to the Administrative Commission, including suggestions about this regulation, especially in relation to points (a), (b), and (c);  
- Carry out any tasks, studies, or assignments given to it by the Administrative Commission.

The Committee is created to help coordinate social security systems across EU countries. Its purpose is to support fair and effective management of social benefits.

